join Groundskeeper 1
if {GroundsKeeper.HasSpoken} == true:
	I don't have anything more to say.
	[end_timeline]
elif {GroundsKeeper.HasSpoken} == false:
	Pray tell, what is happening here?
	Groundskeeper: I’ve opened the old mausoleum, lad. Can you not see?
	Damn. Another body, then.
	Groundskeeper: Mary! Did you bathe in gin?
	My indulgence is mine business. But I do have questions about yours.
label Questions
- Whose mausoleum is this?
	Who reposes within this tomb?
	Groundskeeper: Don’t know and don’t care, son. Some Sharps from years gone by. Spoiled rich folk. End up worm food in their stone coffins.
	They don’t burn the bodies?
	Groundskeeper: No. Got be all right and proper for them Sharps.
	How do you mean?
	Groundskeeper: Are you blind? They fancy themselves above the rest of us. The law. The way things need to be.
	Most struggle throwing their loved ones it a fiery pit.
	Groundskeeper: Yet tis a sacrifice we must all make, lest our swarths rise again and damn the rest of us. But the Sharps? Proper burial. Time to grieve. Bastards.
	set {GroundsKeeper.Q1Answered} = true
	jump Questions
- What do you know of the death?
	Where did they find this body?
	Groundskeeper: Near bonny field. Tis all I know.
	Near that farmhouse where the Glintleys reside?
	Groundskeeper: Aye, lad. Anything else? Work awaits.
	set {GroundsKeeper.Q2Answered} = true
	jump Questions
- Tell me about the grave robbers.
	I see damage, groundskeeper. Chunks cleaved off the stone. What  happened?
	Groundskeeper: There are few  who still come here, let alone those with any respect for them Sharps. No — they come with disdain. Serves them right, ask me.
	Surely you could not condonate such sacrilege?
	Groundskeeper: Tis not my hand that cast the damag, lad. Even more questions for a busy man?
	set {GroundsKeeper.Q3Answered} = true
	jump Questions
- What has happened to this tomb?
	I see there be signs of grave robbers. Any recent activity or incidents?
	Groundskeeper: Of course. Although those who steal from the dead need it more than the frames that once lay here.
	How pragmatic of you.
	Groundskeeper: I’ll have none of your sauce, lad. Ask your questions so I can finish my work.
	set {GroundsKeeper.Q4Answered} = true
	jump Questions
- I should be going. [if {GroundsKeeper.Q1Answered} == true and {GroundsKeeper.Q2Answered} == true and {GroundsKeeper.Q3Answered} == true and {GroundsKeeper.Q4Answered} == true]
	I will take my leave. Gramercy.
	Groundskeeper: Ah, go your ways. That body’s bound to be here anon. To the fields, hunter.
	set {GroundsKeeper.HasSpoken} = true
	[end_timeline]
